#: ../../source/extending/events.rst:2
msgid "Events"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/extending/events.rst:4
msgid ""
"CodeIgniter's Events feature provides a means to tap into and modify the "
"inner workings of the framework without hacking core files. When "
"CodeIgniter runs, it follows a specific execution process. There may be "
"instances, however, when you'd like to cause some action to take place at"
" a particular stage in the execution process. For example, you might want"
" to run a script right before your controllers get loaded, or right "
"after, or you might want to trigger one of your own scripts in some other"
" location."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/extending/events.rst:10
msgid ""
"Events work on a *publish/subscribe* pattern, where an event is triggered"
" at some point during the script execution. Other scripts can "
"\"subscribe\" to that event by registering with the Events class to let "
"it know they want to perform an action when that event is triggered."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/extending/events.rst:19
msgid "Enabling Events"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/extending/events.rst:21
msgid "Events are always enabled, and are available globally."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/extending/events.rst:24
msgid "Defining an Event"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/extending/events.rst:26
msgid ""
"Most events are defined within the **app/Config/Events.php** file. You "
"can subscribe an action to an event with the ``Events`` class's ``on()`` "
"method. The first parameter is the name of the event to subscribe to. The"
" second parameter is a callable that will be run when that event is "
"triggered:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/extending/events.rst:32
msgid ""
"In this example, whenever the ``pre_system`` event is executed, an "
"instance of ``MyClass`` is created and the ``myFunction()`` method is "
"run. Note that the second parameter can be *any* form of `callable "
"<https://www.php.net/manual/en/function.is-callable.php>`_ that PHP "
"recognizes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/extending/events.rst:39
msgid "Setting Priorities"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/extending/events.rst:41
msgid ""
"Since multiple methods can be subscribed to a single event, you will need"
" a way to define in what order those methods are called. You can do this "
"by passing a priority value as the third parameter of the ``on()`` "
"method. Lower values are executed first, with a value of 1 having the "
"highest priority, and there being no limit on the lower values:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/extending/events.rst:47
msgid ""
"Any subscribers with the same priority will be executed in the order they"
" were defined."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/extending/events.rst:49
msgid ""
"Since v4.2.0, three class constants are defined for your use, that set "
"some helpful ranges on the values. You are not required to use these but "
"you might find they aid readability:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/extending/events.rst:54
msgid ""
"The constants ``EVENT_PRIORITY_LOW``, ``EVENT_PRIORITY_NORMAL`` and "
"``EVENT_PRIORITY_HIGH`` has been removed in v4.6.0."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/extending/events.rst:56
msgid ""
"Once sorted, all subscribers are executed in order. If any subscriber "
"returns a boolean false value, then execution of the subscribers will "
"stop."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/extending/events.rst:60
msgid "Publishing your own Events"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/extending/events.rst:62
msgid ""
"The Events library makes it simple for you to create events in your own "
"code, also. To use this feature, you would simply need to call the "
"``trigger()`` method on the **Events** class with the name of the event:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/extending/events.rst:67
msgid ""
"You can pass any number of arguments to the subscribers by adding them as"
" additional parameters. Subscribers will be given the arguments in the "
"same order as defined:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/extending/events.rst:73
msgid "Simulating Events"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/extending/events.rst:75
msgid ""
"During testing, you might not want the events to actually fire, as "
"sending out hundreds of emails a day is both slow and counter-productive."
" You can tell the Events class to only simulate running the events with "
"the ``simulate()`` method. When **true**, all events will be skipped over"
" during the trigger method. Everything else will work as normal, though."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/extending/events.rst:81
msgid "You can stop simulation by passing false:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/extending/events.rst:88
msgid "Event Points"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/extending/events.rst:91
msgid "For Web Apps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/extending/events.rst:93
msgid ""
"The following is a list of available event points for web applications "
"that are invoked by **public/index.php**:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/extending/events.rst:96
msgid ""
"**pre_system** Called early during system execution. The URI, Request, "
"and Response have been instantiated, but page cache checking, routing, "
"and execution of \"before\" controller filters have not yet occurred."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/extending/events.rst:99
msgid ""
"**post_controller_constructor** Called immediately after your controller "
"is instantiated, but prior to any method calls happening."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/extending/events.rst:100
msgid ""
"**post_system** Called right before the final rendered page is sent to "
"the browser, at the end of system execution, after the execution of "
"\"after\" controller filters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/extending/events.rst:106
msgid "For CLI Apps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/extending/events.rst:108
msgid ""
"The following is a list of available event points for "
":doc:`../cli/spark_commands`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/extending/events.rst:110
msgid "**pre_command** Called right before the command code execution."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/extending/events.rst:111
msgid "**post_command** Called right after the command code execution."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/extending/events.rst:114
msgid "Others"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/extending/events.rst:116
msgid ""
"The following is a list of event points available for each of the "
"libraries:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/extending/events.rst:118
msgid ""
"**email** Called after an email sent successfully from "
"``CodeIgniter\\Email\\Email``. Receives an array of the ``Email`` class's"
" properties as a parameter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/extending/events.rst:119
msgid ""
"**DBQuery** Called after a database query whether successful or not. "
"Receives the ``Query`` object."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/extending/events.rst:120
msgid ""
"**migrate** Called after a successful migration call to ``latest()`` or "
"``regress()``. Receives the current properties of ``MigrationRunner`` as "
"well as the name of the method."
msgstr ""

